# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  SECURITY: this project drives real, signed-in financial accounts.
#  Everything below can contain private data or live sessions. Never commit it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Live browser sessions (cookies / auth tokens) — the most dangerous leak
*browser-profile/
browser-profile/
**/*browser-profile*/

# Real per-account config (KEEP the sanitized example)
config.json
config.*.json
!config.example.json

# Downloaded documents — your actual financial records
*.pdf
*.zip

# Runtime state / output
discovery.json
progress.json
new-this-run.txt
run-summary.txt
# sentinel.json is the same class of data as progress.json: it holds the
# identity anchors of a real account - real invoice numbers and their dates -
# plus when that session was last alive. It lands in the working tree on a
# native install, because every shipped config.example.json says
# "output_dir": ".".
sentinel.json
sentinel.json.*
# One file per live session slot, named <provider>.<n>.lock, holding the
# config filename of whoever is running. Natively they land beside the app.
.locks/
# ...and any hand-made copy of them. A file like "discovery.json.pre-fix" or
# "progress.json.bak" holds the same real account data as the original, but
# the exact-name rules above do not cover it - one was nearly committed while
# building a new app.
discovery.json.*
progress.json.*
*.json.bak
*.json.orig
*.csv.bak
*.log
*.csv

# Output / working folders created by the tools
**/Statements/
**/Pay Statements/
**/Tax Documents/
**/Year-End Summaries/
**/Manual Review/
**/Trade Confirmations/
**/Insurance Documents/
**/Other Documents/
**/Receipts/
**/Orders/
**/In-Store/
**/Online/
**/Logs/
**/Diagnostics/
**/Backups/

# Build artifacts (the core wheel is built on demand)
core/dist/
build/

# Python
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/

# OS / editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp

# Verizon browser download temp dir
**/.vz-downloads/

# --- Docker ---------------------------------------------------------------
# The compose environment: holds the browser desktop's password.
.env
# Bind mounts from docker-compose.yml. In order: the signed-in Chrome profile
# (live session cookies), the per-app configs, and every downloaded statement
# plus its state. None of it is ever committable.
/browser-profile/
/config/
/data/

# Claude Code: the shared skills are tracked, per-machine settings are not.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Claude Code worktrees: isolated checkouts, never part of the tree.
.claude/worktrees/
